# gps-raw.js

File: src/data/presets/gps-raw.js (generated: never edited by hand)

From the dataset: gps-raw — Raw GPS pseudoranges of 34 IGS stations on 2025-04-10 (BKG open
  archive): positions solved from the origin, satellites tracked (data/gps/, every input with its
  own .explain)
Inputs:
- data/gps/stations.txt — ours
- data/gps/raw/BRDC.rnx.gz — download
- data/gps/raw/*.crx.gz — download
Collected: 2026-10-02
Licence: other — IGS data, BKG open archive (https://igs.bkg.bund.de): free, cite the IGS
  (Johnston et al. 2017). RNXCMP (crx2rnx): GSI terms, cite Hatanaka (2008).
Sources:
- IGS / BKG GNSS data centre, daily RINEX 3 observation files (30 s) and broadcast ephemeris
  BRDC00IGS, 2025 day 100 <https://igs.bkg.bund.de/root_ftp/IGS/>
- Hatanaka, Y. (2008), A Compression Format and Tools for GNSS Observation Data, Bulletin of the
  Geospatial Information Authority of Japan, 55, 21-30 (RNXCMP)
  <https://terras.gsi.go.jp/ja/crx2rnx.html>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- xyz, lat, lon, h, resid: satellite orbits broadcast in the WGS84 frame, whose scale was fixed by
  stations on the ellipsoid; lat/lon/h on the WGS84 ellipsoid
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Station positions that only solve with kilometre
  residuals, or that fit a plane better than a sphere; pairs of stations that share satellites well
  beyond the geometric separation limit.
Built by: fog build gps-raw
